<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Perth</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Perth is the capital of Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, on the Swan River near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> coast. It was founded in 1829 by Captain James <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a> as the capital of the Swan River Colony and grew slowly until the gold rushes of the 1890s. It is now Australia's fourth-largest city and the centre of the state's mining-based economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/perth.jpg" alt="Perth" width="320" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Perth CBD skyline from State War Memorial Lookout, 2023, 04.jpg: Kgbo derivative work: Georgfotoart · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Perth_CBD_skyline_from_State_War_Memorial_Lookout,_2023,_04_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
